  "identifier": "android-fhir-sdk",
  "name": "Android FHIR SDK",
  "alternateName": [
    "Open Health Stack",
    "Google Open Health Stack"
  ],
  "description": "Google's open-source suite of Kotlin libraries for building offline-capable, mobile-first healthcare applications on Android using the HL7 FHIR standard. Part of the Open Health Stack initiative. Comprises four libraries: FHIR Engine (on-device FHIR resource storage/sync), Structured Data Capture (FHIR Questionnaire rendering), Workflow (CQL-based clinical reasoning), and Knowledge Manager. Apps built on this SDK reach health workers covering 75+ million people across Sub-Saharan Africa and South/Southeast Asia. Apache-2.0, 590 stars, Kotlin, FHIR R4, offline-first with SQLite.",
