  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Google's production-grade Android SDK for offline-capable FHIR mobile apps — the practical choice for building health worker tools in low-connectivity settings. Powers apps reaching 75+ million people across Sub-Saharan Africa and South/Southeast Asia. Apache-2.0, 590 stars, actively maintained with 37 releases. Four modular Kotlin libraries covering data sync, form rendering (FHIR Questionnaires), CQL clinical reasoning, and knowledge management. Kotlin Multiplatform (iOS/web) in alpha as of 2025. Adopt for any mobile FHIR application targeting LMIC or offline-first clinical workflows.",
